Z||000010||StuGood||10-18-2001||12:48 PM||||FWIW, my 1986 V6 SE, purchased new in May, 1986, had an 85mph speedometer (and still does).  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroJoe||10-18-2001||01:16 PM||||Another interesting thing is that the backlit 85 mph speedos, like my friend has in his 86 SE V6, is that there are pegs, so the needle wont register beyond 85.  My 87 coupe 4 cyl had the non backlit 85 in it stock, but I've had the needle past straight down  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Now I have 120 mph backlit gauges and the Aux gauges, and I love them!  The look so much nicer, even with the white faces I had on my old ones.||||reg||1
Z||000012||mrfiero||10-18-2001||02:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroBUZZ:<BR><B>Just to be contrary, My 86 GT has an 85 and my 86 SE has the 120   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Gary</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You (or someone else) must've swapped things around then.  <B>ALL</B> '86-'88 GT's came with the 120 MPH speedo as well as the '87 V-6 SE.  The '86 V-6 SE came with an 85 MPH (same style lettering as the 120) version.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||mshill||10-18-2001||02:18 PM||||skidmark,  I come accross the 120mph instruments about every couple of months.  You have to get to the car in the junkyard when it first arrives or it will be gone in a matter of days if not hours.  They are always the first thing to go.||||reg||1
